\ mandelbrot — Computer Language Benchmarks Game.
\ Escape-time over an N x N grid: c = (2x/N - 1.5) + (2y/N - 1)i, iterate
\ z = z^2 + c up to max-iter times, escaping when |z|^2 > 4. Embarrassingly
\ parallel and branchy (data-dependent iteration count). The checksum is the
\ count of in-set pixels (those that never escape), matching pyperf_mandelbrot.py.

1000 constant n
50 constant max-iter

: in-set? ( cr ci -- flag )
  | >cr >ci zr zi zr2 zi2 iter |
  0.0 to zr  0.0 to zi  0 to iter
  begin iter max-iter < while
    zr zr f* to zr2
    zi zi f* to zi2
    zr2 zi2 f+ 4.0 f> if leave then
    zr zi f* 2.0 f* ci f+ to zi
    zr2 zi2 f- cr f+ to zr
    iter 1+ to iter
  repeat
  iter max-iter >= ;

: run-mandelbrot ( -- count )
  | count x y cr ci |
  0 to count  0 to y
  begin y n < while
    0 to x
    begin x n < while
      x 2.0 f* n f/ 1.5 f- to cr
      y 2.0 f* n f/ 1.0 f- to ci
      cr ci in-set? if count 1+ to count then
      x 1+ to x
    repeat
    y 1+ to y
  repeat
  count ;

now to t0
run-mandelbrot to checksum
now t0 - to elapsed
"elapsed: " . elapsed . " s" . cr
"checksum: " . checksum . cr
bye
